 ## Engine startup
 
 - The engine's `start()` method rejects the returned promise when it cannot bind the configured port, rather than emitting an unhandled error event that would take the process down ([validated by: rejects instead of taking the process down with an unhandled error event](../../src/config.test.ts#L174)).
 
+## A failing `beforeSession`
+
+Owned by re-cinq/HALEngine#94.
+
+- A `beforeSession` that throws reaches the caller as a rejection, as any other failure in the turn does, and fires `onError` with the session and that error ([validated by: runs onError and afterSession when beforeSession throws](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.beforeSession.acceptance.test.ts#L40)).
+- `afterSession` still fires after that throw, so cleanup a deployer placed there runs on the path where allocation failed ([validated by: called even when beforeSession throws](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L172)).
+- A hook that sees such a failure can assume nothing else of the turn happened: no later hook fired and the provider was never called, so `onError` then `afterSession` are the only hooks that run ([validated by: a throw aborts the turn before any later hook or the provider runs](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L116)).
+- `afterSession` receives no signal that the session never started, so it cannot tell "never allocated" from "allocated and finished"; a deployer who allocates in `beforeSession` must make the release in `afterSession` safe for a resource that was never acquired, for example by checking a handle `beforeSession` sets only once it succeeds.
+
 ## Measured semantics — out of scope
 
-These three properties of `src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts` are recorded so the hook features that follow specify against real behaviour. This issue changes none of them; each is a separate, out-of-scope change owned by no issue in this epic.
+These two properties of `src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts` are recorded so the hook features that follow specify against real behaviour. Each is a separate, out-of-scope change owned by no issue in this epic.
 
-- `beforeSession` is awaited before the `try` block opens ([chatOrchestrator.ts#L91](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts#L91)), so a throw there escapes before the `catch`/`finally` exist and skips both `onError` and `afterSession`.
 - The `catch` gates `onError` on `error instanceof Error` ([chatOrchestrator.ts#L150](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts#L150)), so a rejection that is not an `Error` — a thrown string or object — bypasses `onError` entirely while still propagating to the caller.
 - `afterModelResponse` is called once per user message after the round loop exits ([chatOrchestrator.ts#L148](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts#L148)), and is passed the `lastUsage` local — the most recent round's usage, not a sum across tool rounds, so a deployer using the hook for billing or audit under-counts every turn that ran tools.
